From 08e513c0b2889188dce9819bf56c7739300b273d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:33:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: code review 55 fixes, round 3

- EE invocation stacks: when the arena is full, a slot whose invocation
  retired is re-keyed instead of ending the session; exhaustion with every
  slot live logs the slot owners (code-review51 F4 / review 55 C2).
- Memory-card RPC results come from the command that just ran
  (takeMemoryCardCommandResult) instead of a global read afterwards; a
  command that posts nothing is logged and fails (C5).
- ELF segments overlapping the native SDK pools in kernel RAM are refused
  at load; pool bounds live in runtime/ee_kernel_ram.h (C1).
- Generic IOP->EE reverse RPC uses the SDK metadata pointer rule (aligned
  main-RAM aliases) for server, buffer and reply, and logs rejections (C4).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
